# ForgeDeck: docs follow the code

Internal docs live in **`.cursor/docs/`** (not the GitHub landing README). Do not treat them as optional.

After **any** change that users or future developers will notice, update the matching files **in the same PR/commit set**. Shipping code without the docs update is incomplete.

## Always

1. Add a bullet under `CHANGELOG.md` → **Unreleased** (what changed, in the user’s or a developer’s words).
2. Touch the layer file under `.cursor/docs/` if the flow, API, graph, or UX changed — not only when you add a new page.

## Which file

| Kind of change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| New/removed REST or WS message | `.cursor/docs/backend.md` |
| New route, store field, keyboard shortcut | `.cursor/docs/frontend.md`, `.cursor/docs/studio.md` |
| Deck, mixer, FX, key lock, bounce, worklets | `.cursor/docs/audio-engine.md` |
| AI tool, provider, apply path | `.cursor/docs/ai.md` |
| Env var, how to run, tests | `.cursor/docs/development.md` |
| Where to put code / new invariant | `.cursor/docs/conventions.md` |
| Split of browser vs Python | `.cursor/docs/architecture.md` |
| Finished product checkbox | `TODO.md` |
| UX idea not started / started now | `.cursor/docs/roadmap.md` (move off the list when built) |
| Rename, license, “don’t fake GPU/Rubber Band” | `README.md` limitations + conventions |

Index: `.cursor/docs/README.md`. Contributing reminder: `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Do not

- Leave PulseForge in new copy.
- Say Rubber Band landed if only WSOLA remains; say GPU Demucs if only HPSS ran.
- Add docs that contradict the code “for later”.
- Skip CHANGELOG because the diff is “just refactor” if the public behavior or the extension point changed.
- Link `.cursor/docs/` from the public GitHub `README.md` (that page is the product landing).

If you are unsure which doc: update `CHANGELOG.md` and `.cursor/docs/conventions.md` at minimum.
